# Reverse Proxy with NGINX

## Adding new migrations
1. Make sure the new migration env variable mathces `%VARIABLENAME%_MIGRATION_PERCENT` e.g. `MOVIES_MIGRATION_PERCENT`
2. Update envsubst list of variables to parse in Dockerfile (see `CMD envsubst '$MONOLITH_URL $MONOLITH_DOMAIN...` line)
3. Make sure the new migration env variable used as `SPLIT_CLIENT_%VARIABLENAME%_MIGRATION_PERCENT` in NGINX split_clients function (it allows to set the variable as 0 in app config)
3. ⚠️ Make sure that every new migration variable has a upstream "guard":
```
# Define your disable/enable variable (e.g., from a ENV_VARIABLE)
# Default to 0 (normal split) if the disable flag isn't present
map "${GRADUAL_MIGRATION}:${MOVIES_MIGRATION_PERCENT}" $split_mode {
    default           0;
    "~*false:\.*"     0;
    "~*true:0$"       0;
    "~*true:(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$"     1;
}

# Map the mode to your split target
map $split_mode $movies_upstream {
    default     "movies_monolith";
    0           "movies_monolith";      # Override/fallback route
    1           $split_movies_backend;  # Normal route (uses the split_clients below)
}
```

## Why do we need transform_split_clients script?
It allows us to set a migration variable to 0 (0%), creating a **fail-safe copy** of the variable to insert in `split_clients` with a minimum value of 0.01 which is the minimum valid value for `split_clients`.
